<header class="ra-page-head">
  <h1 class="ra-h1">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="ra-lede-dark">What we collect for the read-a-thon, who can see it, and what we do with it. Last updated November 16, 2026.</p>
</header>

<div class="ra-prose">
  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Who we are</h2>
    <p>Resolve to Read is run by the <a href="{{friends_url}}">Friends of the Fiske Free Library</a>, a volunteer nonprofit in Claremont, New Hampshire. We use what you tell us to run the read-a-thon. We never sell it, and we don't use it for advertising.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">What we collect</h2>
    <h3 class="ra-h3">When you sign up</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>The grown-up's email address</b>, so you can sign in on any device.</li>
      <li><b>Your town and state</b>, so we can see which communities the read-a-thon reaches.</li>
      <li><b>For each reader:</b> a first name, whether they're a kid, teen or grown-up, and the year they were born. We don't ask for last names, and kids don't need their own email.</li>
      <li><b>Whether you'd like weekly updates</b> about the read-a-thon. If you say yes, we'll email you once a week during the read-a-thon. You can change your mind any time on your household page.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="ra-h3">While you read</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your reading log: minutes, days, and any titles or formats you choose to add.</li>
      <li>Your goal, bingo squares, teams, prizes picked up, and raffle entries.</li>
      <li>Book recommendations, signed with the first name or nickname you give.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="ra-h3">When you sponsor a reader or give</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name and email for the receipt, the amount, and any name and message you'd like the reader to see.</li>
      <li>Card details go straight to <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe</a>, our payment processor. They never pass through or stay on our site.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Who can see it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Anyone with a reader's sponsor link</b> sees that reader's first name, their minutes, and sponsors' names and messages. The amount is hidden if the sponsor asked for that.</li>
      <li><b>Anyone with a team's link</b> sees the team's name and its members' first names and minutes. Team names, but not members, are listed on the <a href="{{base}}/teams">teams page</a> unless a volunteer hides them.</li>
      <li><b>Everyone</b> sees approved book recommendations with the first name or nickname they were signed with, and the community's total minutes.</li>
      <li><b>Friends volunteers</b> at the library desk see readers' names, household emails, minutes and prizes, so they can add paper logs and hand out prizes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Birth years and towns are never shown publicly. We may share totals that don't identify anyone, like "120 readers from 9 towns", with the library and in our reports.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Services we use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Stripe</b> processes payments.</li>
      <li><b>An email service</b> sends sign-in links and read-a-thon emails for us.</li>
      <li><b>Google Fonts</b> provides the lettering on this site, so Google can see your device's internet address when pages load.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Cookies and your device</h2>
    <p>We use one cookie to keep you signed in. The reading timer saves its start time in your browser so it keeps counting if you close the page. We don't use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Children</h2>
    <p>A grown-up signs up for the household and adds the readers. For children we only collect a first name, the year they were born, and their reading. Kids never need an email address, and we never contact children directly.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Keeping and changing your information</h2>
    <p>The Friends keep read-a-thon records after the event. If you'd like us to correct or remove your household's information, contact us and we'll work it out with you.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ra-card">
    <h2 class="ra-h2">Questions</h2>
    <p>{{#if contact_email}}Email us at <a href="mailto:{{contact_email}}">{{contact_email}}</a>.{{else}}Contact us through the <a href="{{friends_url}}">Friends of the Fiske Free Library</a>.{{/if}} If we change this page, we'll update the date at the top.</p>
  </section>
</div>
